<speak version="1.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis" xml:lang="en-US"><voice name="en-US-EmmaMultilingualNeural">Number seventeen.<break time="1150ms"/></voice><voice name="en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural">The Riverside Science Center will open its space exhibition this Saturday.<break time="180ms"/> The main hall will be available from nine, but the planetarium will remain closed until one because new equipment is being tested.<break time="180ms"/> Visitors with morning planetarium tickets may use them for any afternoon show.<break time="180ms"/> The cafe and gift shop will operate on their normal schedule.<break time="1100ms"/></voice><voice name="en-US-EmmaMultilingualNeural">Question.<break time="350ms"/></voice><voice name="en-US-EmmaMultilingualNeural">What can morning planetarium ticket holders do?</voice></speak>
